The best rainbow is the one after a storm. It appears over the rooftops, with a bright red arch and a soft purple end. It lasts only a few minutes, so I always look up quickly.

My favourite is the one in the garden. It appears when the rain stops and the sun comes out. The colours are so clear that I can see the tiny green leaves and the blue sky through them.

I also like the rainbow that appears in the puddles. It looks like a small bridge made of colour, and it moves when I splash in it.

The rainbow I like most is the one at the end of the day. It appears over the hills, with the sun setting behind it. It looks like a warm blanket of colour, and it makes me feel happy. I wish I could keep one of them forever. [end of text]


